*> The work state of one chunk being generated by steps (core/src/gen-job.cob; research R12): included at level 05 under a
*> group. A job is started (GEN-JOB-START), advanced one step at a time (GEN-JOB-STEP, which does the work of the stage
*> GJ-STAGE at step GJ-SUB of it) and complete when GJ-STAGE is past the last stage; the chunk memory is the job's own
*> until the chunk is installed. The same steps run back to back are the atomic reference (GEN-JOB-RUN-ALL).
*> The generation queue holds one such job (GENQUEUE.cpy GQ-JOB); an atomic generation holds its own.
    05 GJ-ACTIVE            BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-DIM               BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-CX                BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-CZ                BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-STAGE             BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-SUB               BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-STEPS             BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-ADDR              USAGE POINTER.
    05 GJ-FINAL-ROOT        BINARY-LONG.
*>  heightmaps: the y of the highest recorded block, -65 for an empty column; index z * 16 + x + 1
    05 GJ-HEIGHTS.
       10 GJ-HM-SURFACE     BINARY-LONG OCCURS 256 TIMES.
       10 GJ-HM-OCEAN       BINARY-LONG OCCURS 256 TIMES.
    05 GJ-GRID.
       COPY GENGRID.
*>  the aquifer of the chunk (aquifer.cob): READY 0 = no aquifer data (the global fluid picker alone), the positional factory
*>  of minecraft:aquifer, skipSamplingAboveY, the noise handles and density roots it uses, the grid cells (3 x 3 columns of
*>  cells from chunk x - 1 and chunk z - 1, 35 layers from cell y -7: centre and status, computed on first use) and the memo
*>  of the preliminary surface level by quart column
    05 GJ-AQ.
       10 GJ-AQ-READY       BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-FLO         BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
       10 GJ-AQ-FHI         BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
       10 GJ-AQ-SKIP-Y      BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-MAX-SURFACE BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-BARRIER     BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-FLOOD       BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-SPREAD      BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-LAVA        BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-ROOT-PSL    BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-ROOT-ERO    BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-ROOT-DEP    BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-CELL OCCURS 315 TIMES.
          15 GJ-AQ-HAVE     BINARY-LONG.
          15 GJ-AQ-PX       BINARY-LONG.
          15 GJ-AQ-PY       BINARY-LONG.
          15 GJ-AQ-PZ       BINARY-LONG.
          15 GJ-AQ-STAT     BINARY-LONG.
          15 GJ-AQ-LEVEL    BINARY-LONG.
          15 GJ-AQ-TYPE     BINARY-LONG.
       10 GJ-AQ-SURF OCCURS 2048 TIMES.
          15 GJ-AQ-S-USED   BINARY-LONG.
          15 GJ-AQ-S-X      BINARY-LONG.
          15 GJ-AQ-S-Z      BINARY-LONG.
          15 GJ-AQ-S-VALUE  BINARY-LONG.
*>  the surface stage (surface.cob): the preliminary surface level at the chunk's four corners (10 section 6.3, north-west, north-east,
*>  south-west, south-east) and the biome ids (plus 1, 0 = not computed) of the quart cells of the 6 x 6 columns around the chunk
*>  at each of the 96 quart layers (index layer * 36 + (qz + 1) * 6 + qx + 2, qx and qz relative to the chunk's first quart cell)
    05 GJ-SF.
       10 GJ-SF-CSL         FLOAT-LONG OCCURS 4 TIMES.
       10 GJ-SF-RING        BINARY-LONG OCCURS 3456 TIMES.
